  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-11T15:15:26.322Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It takes ~1 frame to snap a cursor forward after inserting a character.\n\nAt a first glance this doesn't seem to be an issue.. Until a moment that your performance becomes inconsistent, (common in populated lobbies) which makes it possible to press a new key before the \"cursor snap\" ever finishes.\n\nThis can causes a cursor to go in a backwards direction, leaving a previous symbol in the front.. Continuing to type your sentence - you will eventually realize that your words are missing one or several letters that got moved all the way to the very end of the message.\n\nVideo: https://youtu.be/bgBfrpgUyec\n\nEdit: Replaced video link because it went unavailable.",
